          "author_profile_url": null,
          "date": "December 07, 2012, 12:07:20 PM",
          "date_raw": "\u00ab on: December 07, 2012, 12:07:20 PM \u00bb",
          "post_text": "What steps do you take to efficiently work these reports? How often do you work them?",
          "post_text_chars": 85,
          "location": null,
          "poster_fields_present": [
            "membergroup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "thread_id": "6999",
          "category": "Billing",
          "post_id": "20755",
          "post_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php/topic,6999.msg20755.html#msg20755",
          "author_name": "Michele",
          "author_type": "registered",
          "author_id": "3",
          "author_profile_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php?action=profile;u=3",
          "date": "December 10, 2012, 10:31:50 AM",
          "date_raw": "\u00ab Reply #1 on: December 10, 2012, 10:31:50 AM \u00bb",
          "post_text": "We run aging reports (and work them) on all claims over 30 days every 4-6 wks. We do patient billing every month.",
          "post_text_chars": 113,
          "location": null,
          "poster_fields_present": [
            "membergroup",
            "postcount",
            "postgroup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "thread_id": "6999",
          "category": "Billing",
          "post_id": "20784",
          "post_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php/topic,6999.msg20784.html#msg20784",
          "author_name": "rmk123",
          "author_type": "guest",
          "author_id": null,
          "author_profile_url": null,
          "date": "December 11, 2012, 12:05:21 PM",
          "date_raw": "\u00ab Reply #2 on: December 11, 2012, 12:05:21 PM \u00bb",
          "post_text": "Right.....do you sort by largest balance to smallest, by financial class, etc. for time sake or simply go down the list?",
          "post_text_chars": 120,
          "location": null,
          "poster_fields_present": [
            "membergroup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "thread_id": "6999",
          "category": "Billing",
          "post_id": "20796",
          "post_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php/topic,6999.msg20796.html#msg20796",
          "author_name": "Michele",
          "author_type": "registered",
          "author_id": "3",
          "author_profile_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php?action=profile;u=3",
          "date": "December 12, 2012, 09:58:17 AM",
          "date_raw": "\u00ab Reply #3 on: December 12, 2012, 09:58:17 AM \u00bb",
          "post_text": "Our reports sort by insurance carrier, then alphabetically. It also classifies it by age as well. I do not sort by size of balance.",
          "post_text_chars": 131,
          "location": null,
          "poster_fields_present": [
            "membergroup",
            "postcount",
            "postgroup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "thread_id": "6999",
          "category": "Billing",
          "post_id": "20798",
          "post_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php/topic,6999.msg20798.html#msg20798",
          "author_name": "PMRNC",
          "author_type": "registered",
          "author_id": "488",
          "author_profile_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php?action=profile;u=488",
          "date": "December 12, 2012, 10:24:45 AM",
          "date_raw": "\u00ab Reply #4 on: December 12, 2012, 10:24:45 AM \u00bb",
          "post_text": "Quote Our reports sort by insurance carrier, then alphabetically. It also classifies it by age as well. I do not sort by size of balance. I do it the same way (GMTA) After 90 days I produce a report with an internal classification that shows the doctors which accounts should be sent for further collection to a collection agency or service. I have three different classification codes I use to report to my clients and they review and make final determination and then I change the classification according to their decision. Very organized and I know where every balance is.",
          "post_text_chars": 576,
          "location": null,
          "poster_fields_present": [
            "postcount",
            "postgroup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "thread_id": "6999",
          "category": "Billing",
          "post_id": "20825",
          "post_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php/topic,6999.msg20825.html#msg20825",
          "author_name": "rmk123",
          "author_type": "guest",
          "author_id": null,
          "author_profile_url": null,
          "date": "December 13, 2012, 05:56:22 PM",
          "date_raw": "\u00ab Reply #5 on: December 13, 2012, 05:56:22 PM \u00bb",
          "post_text": "Thanks for your replies.",
          "post_text_chars": 24,
          "location": null,
          "poster_fields_present": [
            "membergroup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "thread_id": "6999",
          "category": "Billing",
          "post_id": "20828",
          "post_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php/topic,6999.msg20828.html#msg20828",
          "author_name": "Christy",
          "author_type": "registered",
          "author_id": "30102",
          "author_profile_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php?action=profile;u=30102",
          "date": "December 13, 2012, 07:28:08 PM",
          "date_raw": "\u00ab Reply #6 on: December 13, 2012, 07:28:08 PM \u00bb",
          "post_text": "it's good to work the reports by payor, this way when you call an ins carrier to follow up, you can call on several patients at the same time.",
          "post_text_chars": 142,
          "location": null,
          "poster_fields_present": [
            "postcount",
            "postgroup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "thread_id": "6999",
          "category": "Billing",
          "post_id": "20834",
          "post_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php/topic,6999.msg20834.html#msg20834",
          "author_name": "DMK",
          "author_type": "registered",
          "author_id": "5441",
          "author_profile_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php?action=profile;u=5441",
          "date": "December 14, 2012, 01:26:48 PM",
          "date_raw": "\u00ab Reply #7 on: December 14, 2012, 01:26:48 PM \u00bb",
          "post_text": "By working by payer you can also see who the slow payers are, so you're not so worried about those accounts.",
          "post_text_chars": 108,
          "location": null,
          "poster_fields_present": [
            "postcount",
            "postgroup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "thread_id": "6999",
          "category": "Billing",
          "post_id": "21005",
          "post_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php/topic,6999.msg21005.html#msg21005",
          "author_name": "rmk123",
          "author_type": "guest",
          "author_id": null,
          "author_profile_url": null,
          "date": "January 07, 2013, 11:28:14 PM",
          "date_raw": "\u00ab Reply #8 on: January 07, 2013, 11:28:14 PM \u00bb",
          "post_text": "Good points -- thank you!",
          "post_text_chars": 25,
          "location": null,
