          "author_profile_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php?action=profile;u=373",
          "date": "June 16, 2009, 06:38:41 PM",
          "date_raw": "\u00ab on: June 16, 2009, 06:38:41 PM \u00bb",
          "post_text": "Hi Michele, I was wondering I know now that when you bill for a optometrist you had said you bill the office visit to Medicare and the glasses to DMERC, but in my software there is not a option to choose this type of billing center. When you set up the patient you have to enter primary, secondary and ter. and then when you create a claim you choose from a drop down list of their ins co, I do not see a way to choose DMERC, do you have any tips on what you do in your software. margemib",
          "post_text_chars": 488,
          "location": null,
          "poster_fields_present": [
            "postcount",
            "postgroup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "thread_id": "1706",
          "category": "Billing",
          "post_id": "4115",
          "post_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php/topic,1706.msg4115.html#msg4115",
