          "author_type": "registered",
          "author_id": "488",
          "author_profile_url": "https://www.medicalbillinglive.com/members/index.php?action=profile;u=488",
          "date": "June 18, 2009, 11:44:27 AM",
          "date_raw": "\u00ab Reply #18 on: June 18, 2009, 11:44:27 AM \u00bb",
          "post_text": "If it were my software I would want to know if it's an \"option\" or a \"work-around\" and also look at what the standard is and find out why that feature is not standard in your software. There were many instances I needed to switch carriers on a claim by claim basis! the only work around I can see for a software that doesn't allow this is to delete one carrier, add the other and re-add it later on ..but that surely isn't productive or efficient.",
